<%= content[:page_title] %>
==============
<% content[:event_payloads].each do |payload| %>
<h2 id="<%= payload.fetch("name") %>"><%= payload.fetch("name") %></h2>

**Definition:** <%= payload.fetch("definition") %>

<%   if payload.fetch("trigger", nil).present? %>
**Trigger:** <%= payload.fetch("trigger") %>
<%   end %>

<%   payload.fetch("examples").each do |example| %>
<%   if example.fetch("description", nil).present? %>
**Description:** <%= example.fetch("description") %>
<%   end %>

### Payload Example:

```json
<%= JSON.pretty_generate(example.fetch("payload")) %>
```

<%   end %>

<%   unless payload.fetch("schema").empty? %>
### Event Body Schema

| Field | Description |
|-|-|
<%     payload.fetch("schema").each do |field, description| %>
| **<%= field %>** | <%= description %> |
<%     end %>
<%   end %>
<% end %>

Note: Timestamps will be in ISO8601 format, including an offset. Be sure to take that into account when parsing, since it’s unspecified which offset timestamps will use, and the offset may even change between different timestamps within a single event.
